=encoding utf8

=head1 NAME

std/tui - Terminal UI helpers.

=head1 SYNOPSIS

  from std/tui import supports_ansi, colour_text, readline, write_line;

  write_line( "Warning", "yellow" );
  let path := readline( "File: ", "", filename_completions );

=head1 DESCRIPTION

This runtime-supported module provides small terminal UI primitives for
standard-library modules that need command-line fallbacks.

=head1 EXPORTED FUNCTIONS

=over

=item * C<ansi_esc()>

Returns a one-character ANSI escape string.

=item * C<supports_ansi()>

Returns true when stdout appears to be an ANSI-capable terminal.

=item * C<colour_text(text, colour)>

Returns C<text> wrapped in ANSI colour escapes when C<supports_ansi()> is
true, otherwise returns C<text> unchanged. Supported colours include
C<black>, C<red>, C<green>, C<yellow>, C<blue>, C<magenta>, C<cyan>, and
C<white>.

=item * C<write(text, colour)>

Writes C<text> to stdout, optionally coloured.

=item * C<write_line(text, colour)>

Writes C<text> followed by a newline to stdout, optionally coloured.

=item * C<readline(prompt, default, completion_callback)>

Reads a line from stdin after displaying C<prompt>. C<completion_callback>
may be C<null> or a function. The callback receives the string entered so
far and returns an Array of possible completions.

=item * C<readline_supports_completion()>

Returns true when the runtime can provide native readline completion.

=item * C<filename_completions(text)>

Returns path completions for C<text>.

=item * C<directory_completions(text)>

Returns directory completions for C<text>.

=back

